    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15627" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēmĕrĭta</span></b> ,
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Lusitania</i>, now <i>Merida</i>, Mela, 2, 6, 4; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 41,
				65, § 141</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēmĕrĭtānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of
				Emerita</i>, Murat. Inscr. 1550, 1.— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ēmĕrĭtensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of Emerita</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conventus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 22, 35, § 117</span></i>
			.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Emeri-tenses</span></b> ,
				ium, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Emerita</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 1,
			78</span></i>.</div>
